{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Adopt Java 17+ as the target language version, consistent with Spring Framework 6.0 requirements.",
    "Model the Admin SPI as a Java interface (Admin SPI) with operations getStatus(ModuleDescriptor), listModules(), and a Map<ModuleDescriptor.Key, ModuleStatus> accessor; concrete implementations are bound via Spring profiles.",
    "Introduce a new Module Registry abstraction package (e.g., org.springframework.xd.admin.spi and org.springframework.xd.module.registry) that decouples the SPI from its concrete providers.",
    "Create a dedicated repository/directory (e.g., spring-xd-admin-spi) to host all Admin SPI implementations and their tests, satisfying the 'permanent location' user story.",
    "Use Spring Boot @Profile-based conditional configuration (@ConditionalOnProperty / @Profile) to select the active Admin SPI implementation at runtime for 'java -jar admin', 'cf push admin', and 'ltc create admin'.",
    "Reuse Spring Cloud Netflix Eureka client for module self-registration; each module publishes metadata (name, coordinates, status) on installation as an Eureka instance.",
    "Extend Eureka metadata storage with module-specific key/value pairs (module name, type, descriptor URI) so the repository can answer queries beyond spring.application.name.",
    "Provide a name-based search capability in the Module Registry that delegates to a Eureka-aware repository and/or a local index, while keeping spring.application.name as the default key.",
    "Use Maven multi-module layout so the new abstraction, SPI implementations, and Eureka integration can evolve independently and be reused across Spring XD and s-c-s."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Developer's familiarity with Spring XD, Spring Cloud Skipper (s-c-s), and Spring Cloud Netflix Eureka is average; no dedicated ramp-up time is included beyond the design phase.",
    "External systems (Receptor, Cloud Foundry CloudController, Eureka) are accessible in a test environment; mock servers are sufficient where live endpoints are not available.",
    "Module descriptor and module status data models already exist in the Spring XD codebase; only the SPI-facing API needs to be defined or refined.",
    "No major refactoring of existing Spring XD admin code is required beyond introducing the abstraction layer and profile wiring.",
    "All work is performed by a single mid-to-senior developer working in isolation; no coordination overhead with other team members is included.",
    "Unit, integration, and end-to-end tests are part of the same increment; lightweight test scaffolding (e.g., embedded Eureka, stubbed Controller/Receptor clients) is used.",
    "Effort is measured in productive work-hours, excluding meetings, code reviews outside the developer's own work, and unrelated maintenance.",
    "Documentation is limited to inline Javadoc and a short README for the new repo; no separate user guide is produced."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and high-level design",
      "activity_description": "Review all eight user stories, clarify the Admin SPI surface (getStatus, listModules, status map), define the module registry abstraction responsibilities, and decide on profile and Eureka integration points. Produce a short design note consumed by the implementation activities.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Set up dedicated SPI implementation repository (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Create a new Maven module/repository dedicated to Admin SPI implementations, configure parent POM, dependency management for Spring XD, Spring Cloud, and Eureka, and add shared test fixtures so future contributors can easily extend coverage.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement module registry abstraction (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Define the ModuleDescriptor and ModuleStatus types, the Admin SPI interface, and a base/abstract ModuleRegistry implementation that can be subclassed by SPI providers. Include Javadoc and basic unit tests establishing the contract for downstream implementations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Implement Receptor Admin SPI (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Develop a Receptor-backed Admin SPI that resolves deployed Spring XD modules via the Receptor API and implements getStatus, listModules, and the status map. Include a Receptor client wrapper, error handling, and integration tests using a stubbed Receptor endpoint.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Implement CloudController Admin SPI (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Develop a Cloud Foundry CloudController-backed Admin SPI that enumerates apps/modules via the Cloud Controller API and exposes the same three operations as U1. Include a CF client wrapper, paging/token handling, and integration tests with a mock CloudController.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Make SPI implementations profile-aware (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Wire each Admin SPI implementation behind a Spring profile (e.g., 'receptor', 'cloudcontroller', 'default') using @Profile / @Conditional annotations, so the right implementation is auto-selected for 'java -jar admin', 'cf push admin', and 'ltc create admin'. Add a small configuration test that verifies bean selection per profile.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Implement Eureka-based module self-registration (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Hook the module installation flow so that newly installed Spring XD / s-c-s modules register themselves as Eureka instances. Configure the Eureka client, define registration triggers, and add integration tests using an embedded Eureka server to confirm instances appear and disappear as modules are installed/removed.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Store module metadata in Eureka (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Extend the Eureka registration to carry module-specific metadata (module name, type, descriptor location, version) in the instance metadata map, and expose a repository abstraction that reads this metadata to derive the current module state. Include unit tests for the repository's metadata parsing logic.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Implement name-based module search (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Extend the module registry/repository with a search-by-name capability (in addition to spring.application.name). Implement an in-memory index backed by Eureka instance metadata and provide a simple lookup API plus tests covering exact and partial name matches.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "End-to-end integration and validation",
      "activity_description": "Run cross-cutting integration tests that exercise the full flow: module installation -> Eureka self-registration -> metadata storage -> Admin SPI query via both Receptor and CloudController profiles -> name-based search. Fix integration defects and harden error handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and developer onboarding notes",
      "activity_description": "Add Javadoc on the Admin SPI and module registry APIs, a README in the new SPI repository explaining how to add a new implementation, and brief notes on the profile conventions and Eureka metadata keys.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 224
  }
}
```

